<title>GERMANY: West German April adjusted jobless rises 6,000.</title>
<headline>West German April adjusted jobless rises 6,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>				 Apr 97	  Mar 97	   Apr 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    3.031 mln     3.127 mln	2.769 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		3.016 mln     3.010 mln	2.745 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+6,000	  UNCHANGED	n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		9.8  pct	10.2 pct	 9.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	173,407	 210,050	  285,965</p>
<p> Vacancies		   204,809	 241,660	  311,070</p>
<p>Change in number in work Feb 97	  Jan 96</p>
<p>				 -47,000	 -77,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
